    "updated_at": "2026-11-16T16:34:09Z",
    "body": "STOPPED: claim released after a repeated real gate failure.\n\nThe bug reproduces on upstream/main e3ca44fa7. The mount wrappers, cam.post, and MCP post each wrote one combined program with per_op enabled.\n\nA seven-line guard in posting_mounts.rs refuses per_op by name before combined posting. All three new tests pass with the guard. Restoring upstream/main posting_mounts.rs makes all three fail. Restoring the guard makes all three pass again. No NC or CL goldens changed.\n\nThe quick gate fails in first_4axis_part::the_committed_project_posts_the_committed_program at tests/first_4axis_part.rs:60. The machine check says Flat A-90 inputs moved since generation and requires regeneration before posting. This happens before the new guard. An exact rerun fails with the same error. I left that fixture unchanged. The remaining gate was stopped under the worker stop rule.\n\nThe patch and pinning tests remain in .claude/worktrees/issue-2188 on issue/2188-per-op-post-guard. Nothing was committed or pushed. No PR was opened. Failure and mutation logs remain in /tmp/2188-*.txt. The issue is free again.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
