    "updated_at": "2026-11-16T19:13:40Z",
    "body": "Thank you again for this report. It is fixed in `main` by PR #2203.\n\nWith \"one program per operation\" on, the post now writes a separate program file for each operation. The whole job is checked before any file is written. The combined-program paths refuse this option by name, so the second setup can no longer run directly after the first setup with no stop.\n\nThe fix ships in the next release (v0.23.0). You can test it now with a build from `main`.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
